WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.200
Git + Git LFS. One companion.

00:04.200 --> 00:06.800
Find your workflow. Nine categories group useful commands by intent.

00:06.800 --> 00:08.600
Save your work: stage, commit and stash.

00:08.600 --> 00:10.400
Try ideas: switch, merge and rebase.

00:10.400 --> 00:12.200
Large files: track, transfer and verify with Git LFS.

00:12.200 --> 00:14.000
Reclaim space: preview, prune and clean.

00:14.000 --> 00:17.000
Learn the map. A practical command library to explore at your own pace.

00:17.000 --> 00:19.400
Search every workflow by task, command or flag.

00:19.400 --> 00:23.200
Start typing. Press Tab to accept autocomplete. You choose when to run.

00:23.200 --> 00:25.500
Review the real command before execution.

00:25.500 --> 00:28.100
Run it. See real output and a clear result.

00:28.100 --> 00:30.300
Preview cleanup with git lfs prune --dry-run.

00:30.300 --> 00:32.300
Every action has a short plain-language hint.

00:32.300 --> 00:35.500
Expand examples to learn what a command means.

00:35.500 --> 00:38.000
74 curated actions. 148 expandable examples. Explore before you execute.

00:38.000 --> 00:40.000
Look around. Share and sync. Recover. Set up.

00:40.000 --> 00:42.300
Windows, macOS and Linux. Run setup, reopen your terminal, type git-companion.

00:42.300 --> 00:46.000
Git Companion. Find it. Learn it. Run it.
